      "title": "University Of Rhode Island: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.uri.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs University Of Rhode Island: All Jobs 2026-09-04T11:59:25-04:00 https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17032 2026-09-04T11:59:24-04:00 2026-09-04T11:59:25-04:00 Landscape Maintenance Technician III <div>GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: Within the University of Rhode Island (URI), to perform and oversee advanced technical and skilled work, including computation of quantities, quality, cost, estimating labor and materials relating to landscape projects at URI and all the properties owned by URI; to be responsible for and train subordinates on: maintenance of equipment, the application of general use pesticides, professional tree work, planting, watering, sweeping, snow removal, and the utilization of plants used to beautify the university properties; and to do related work as required.<br><br>SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Works under the general supervision of a superior with the expectation of independent decision-making and exercising sound judgement in the application of the practices and techniques of the trade; work may be reviewed upon completion.<br><br>SUPERVISION EXERCISED: To supervise, assign, lay out and review the work of staff engaged in the university landscape maintenance program.</div> Landscape & Grounds Maintenance https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16862 2026-07-20T15:35:08-04:00 2026-07-20T15:35:09-04:00 Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by September14, 2026. Applications received after September 14, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<strong><br></strong><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:</strong><br><br>Ensure that student behavior aligns with and supports the University’s mission by investigating and adjudicating community standards violations both on and off campus. Provide proactive education and outreach to the campus community on topics related to community standards. Be responsible for comprehensive case management, data analysis, and the development of educational initiatives aimed at promoting a respectful and safe community environment.</div><div><br></div> VP Student Affrs. https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16715 2026-05-27T08:26:42-04:00 2026-05-27T08:26:43-04:00 Associate Dean for Clinical and Health Promotion Programs <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by July 1, 2026. Applications received after July 1, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:<br></strong><br></div><div>Provide strategic leadership as a key member of the College's Administrative Leadership Team, overseeing all aspects of clinical and health promotion programs in partnership with the Dean.</div><div>To advance the College’s mission in the area of health sciences education and community impact, the Associate Dean will champion excellence in existing clinical and health promotion programs, while helping to lead strategic planning to expand, innovate and enhance the College’s initiatives in the area of clinical services and health promotion.<br><br></div> Dean Health Sciences https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16995 2026-08-27T10:17:09-04:00 2026-08-27T10:17:10-04:00 Coordinator, Memorial Union Scheduling and Event Services <div><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:<br></strong><br></div><div>Coordinate Memorial Union event scheduling and logistical support through effective collaboration among departments within the Memorial Union (Operations, Housekeeping, Building Services, etc.), with on-campus and off-campus stakeholders, and with students. Foster enhanced community engagement through coordination of university services and technology in regards to events, information and scheduling while maintaining excellent customer service.</div><div><br><br></div> Scheduling & Information Ctr https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17036 2026-09-04T14:09:42-04:00 2026-09-04T14:09:42-04:00 Cook's Helper (Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year) Dining Central Operations https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16874 2026-07-24T11:29:50-04:00 2026-07-24T11:29:50-04:00 Hall Director II (2 positions) <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by June 25, 2026. Applications received after June 25, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:<br></strong><br></div><div>Serve as chief administrative officer for residence hall(s) housing up to 900 students, on a 24-hour basis. Develop and coordinate educational, cultural, social, and recreational programs with the objective of fostering student development and encouraging a sense of community within the living units. Supervise and train student support staff. Establish and enforce policies and regulations as designated by the University, division, and department. Assist with student adjudication. Serve as liaison on issues of building maintenance and custodial services. Perform various other administrative functions. This is a live-in, twelve month position.<br><br></div> HRL Central Office https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16767 2026-06-15T12:55:52-04:00 2026-06-15T12:55:53-04:00 Full Professor of Psychology (Digital Health) <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled.</strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by August 15, 2026. Applications received after August 15, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>_______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br></div><div><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State's flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________</div><div><br></div><div>The Department of Psychology at the University of Rhode Island has embarked on a cluster hiring strategy in the domain of digital health broadly. We are inviting applications for a tenured position at the Full Professor level, with 2 two tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor level being recruited in a separate announcement. We seek scholars whose work leverages digital health technologies-including wearable devices (e.g., Fitbit), smartphone-based assessments, mobile health interventions (e.g., just-in-time adaptive interventions), Al-driven tools, and mobile sensing-to advance innovative approaches to assessment, prevention, and intervention.<br><br></div><div>Successful applicants will have an established an outstanding scholarly record that demonstrates the ability to develop and lead an independent research program supported by NIH or other extramural funding. The ideal candidates will contribute to the mission of the Behavioral Science and/or Clinical program areas by: 1) Conducting impactful digital health research that applies cutting-edge methodologies or develops novel computational and quantitative approaches aligned with and complementary to departmental strengths (e.g., substance use, health equity, community-engaged research, mental health, child health); 2) teaching quantitative methods and/or content courses that are essential to the undergraduate and graduate training, 3) incorporating justice, equity, diversity, and inclusion (JEDI) principles into their research, teaching, and service. It is anticipated that one position will be filled in the Behavioral Science program area and one in the Clinical Psychology program area. We are particularly interested in candidates with strong methodological expertise in areas such as statistical modeling, machine learning, intensive longitudinal data analysis, micro-randomized trial design, natural language processing, Al applications in digital health, and real-world data analysis. Successful candidates will leverage these approaches to develop and evaluate data-driven healthcare solutions.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Psychology houses among the largest undergraduate and graduate programs at the University, with over 1000 undergraduates and 60 graduate students. We offer both BA and BS Undergraduate degrees, doctoral tracks in Behavioral Science and an APA-accredited Clinical Psychology program, and a new masters-level program in Mental and Behavioral Health Counseling. Clinical training is supported by our Psychological Consultation Center (PCC) that serves both the university and the larger Rhode Island community. For more information about the Department of Psychology, please visit <strong>https://web.uri.edu/psychology/</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The Department, College, and University recognize that the field of psychology is strengthened by contributions from a broad range of perspectives. The Department of Psychology is committed to creating measurable, lasting change within the field using justice, equity, diversity, inclusion, and access <strong>(https://web.uri.edu/ Psychologyjedi-statement)/ </strong>as guiding principles. As such, we encourage applicants from groups that are historically underrepresented in the field of psychology who will support the missions of the Department, College, and University to expose students to different perspectives and share in community building. We seek applicants who are experienced in teaching and mentoring students and faculty in ways that include and support individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds. Further, we encourage applicants with leadership experience in initiatives related to justice, equity, diversity, inclusion, and access.<br><br><strong>Qualifications<br><br>Required:<br></strong><br></div><div>1. A PhD (or equivalent) in psychology or a closely related field.<br><br></div><div>2. A highly productive record of research that is recognized internationally for excellence and innovation including a highly cited record of publications in major journals in their field.<br><br></div><div>3. Demonstrated success in obtaining external funding that will support productive research in digital health technologies.<br><br></div><div>4. Demonstrated commitment to JEDI through research, teaching, and/or service activities.<br><br></div><div>5. Demonstrated ability in teaching and mentoring graduate and/or undergraduate students.<br><br></div><div>6. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills.<br><br></div><div>7. Demonstrated proficiency in oral communication skills.<br><br></div><div>8. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations.<br><br><strong>Preferred:</strong></div><div><br></div><div>1. Research specialization that includes the application of cutting-edge methods or development of new computational and quantitative approaches in domains relevant to digital health.<br><br></div><div>2. Demonstrated ability to teach quantitative methods and/or content courses that are critical to the undergraduate and graduate training.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>EEO Statement:<br></strong><br></div><div>URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711.<br><br></div> Psychology https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17003 2026-08-28T00:01:50-04:00 2026-08-28T00:01:50-04:00 HIGHER EDUCATION ADMINISTRATIVE ASSISTANT I <div>GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES:<br>Within a college/university system, to perform routine administrative support functions in an academic department utilizing college enterprise software systems with common business applications and a wide variety of office equipment and computer software applications including word processing, spreadsheets and other contemporary office programs and equipment; and to do related work as required.<br>SUPERVISION RECEIVED:<br>Works under the general supervision of an academic department chair, Dean and/or senior faculty member; specific tasks may be given directly by a variety of professionals; instructions usually are given only at the beginning of assignments involving a new type of work; work is generally in final form when compared and is subject to, but does not always receive, review by supervisors. SUPERVISION EXERCISED: None</div> Business&Economics ResearchCtr https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16478 2026-03-18T14:15:13-04:00 2026-03-18T14:15:14-04:00 PART-TIME FACULTY: Art and Art History - (UI Graduate Certificate Program) <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position is filled.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________</strong></div><div>Qualified candidates who are not selected for employment for fall semester 2024 will have their applications remain active for two (2) years should a future opportunity arise during the 2025–2026 instructional year, September 1, 2025–August 31, 2026.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Art and Art History in the College of Arts and Sciences seeks part-time faculty to teach online graduate courses for the UI Graduate Certificate Program on a per-course basis. Areas of instruction include UI Design Styling and Prototyping, UI Motion Design, UI Information Visualization, and UI Design Principles.<br><br></div><div>As the largest college at the University of Rhode Island, the College of Arts and Sciences brings together and supports undergraduate programs across the arts, humanities, sciences, and social sciences. The college is committed to excellence in teaching and its academic units create learning experiences that stress the free and rigorous pursuit of knowledge, intellectual curiosity, respect for differences across cultures and perspectives, a passion for personal expression, and an investment in the responsibilities of an educated global citizen in a democratic society. The College facilitates students' development into leaders and global citizens who think critically and creatively, communicate effectively, and participate actively in local and global communities.<br><br></div><div><strong>Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><div><br></div><div>A selected candidate will teach one (1) or two (2) courses in the Department of Art and Art History. Courses are asynchronous and delivered in an accelerated 7-week format. Part-time faculty are not required to engage in research or service activities but must hold regular office hours and be available to assist students enrolled in their courses. They are expected to stay current in their fields of instruction and with pedagogical methods and instructional technologies. Online teaching requires certification and possibly training by the University. Courses are three (3) credits.<br><br></div><div><strong>Specific Responsibilities Include:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Delivering engaging and interactive online lessons and assignments on UI Design principles, tools, and techniques through our course management platform (Brightspace)</li><li>Providing regular feedback, guidance, and mentoring support to students to facilitate their learning and skill development while conveying confidence in every student's ability to learn</li><li>Cultivating a collaborative and participatory online learning environment that values diversity of people, ideas, cultures, and forms of expression</li><li>Evaluating student performance and progress, and providing timely assessment</li><li>Staying updated on industry trends, best practices, and emerging technologies in User Interface Design.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Qualifications</strong><br><br><strong>Required:<br></strong><br></div><div>1. Candidates must have a master's degree in Design, Computer Science, Human-Computer Interaction, or related field or a bachelor's degree and three (3) years of professional experience in areas such as UI Design Styling and Prototyping, UI Motion Design, UI Information Visualization, and UI Design Principles, Wireframing/Prototyping, and/or content optimization and strategy.<br><br></div><div>2. Candidates should have technical knowledge and proficiency in interaction design technologies (e.g., Figma, Sketch, XD) and the Adobe Suite, as well as remote collaboration tools.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Preferred:<br></strong><br></div><div>1. Previous teaching or instructional experience at college level, particularly in an online or remote setting.<br><br></div><div>2. For candidates with master’s degrees, professional experience in the field of UI<br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>The University of Rhode Island is an equal-opportunity employer. It is the policy of the University of Rhode Island to provide reasonable accommodation when requested by a qualified applicant or employee with a disability. </strong><br><br></div> Arts & Art History https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16885 2026-07-27T14:55:18-04:00 2026-07-27T14:55:19-04:00 Professor, Nursing <div><br><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong><br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<strong><br><br>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<strong><br></strong><br><br>The College of Nursing is searching for a tenure-track Professor to begin Fall 2026.<br><br></div><div><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The URI College of Nursing is committed to scientific inquiry, knowledge development, and excellence in teaching. We are building a robust research portfolio and are known for our innovative undergraduate and graduate programs that support our mission to prepare nurses to excel as outstanding clinicians, scholars, and leaders who will enhance the health and health care of individuals, families, communities, and populations both locally and globally. We seek a dynamic faculty member to join us as we continue to grow. The successful candidate will have an appointment with the College of Nursing with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the campus and external partners. The candidate will serve as a senior member of the faculty and will be expected to have a program of research supported by extramural funding in an area that complements the mission of the College of Nursing. The successful candidate will also contribute to the University’s teaching mission and participate in service activities.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Contribute to the undergraduate and graduate teaching mission of the University by mentoring students and teaching courses for the college.</li><li>Maintain a robust program of research germane to nursing and health that is extramurally funded.</li><li>Maintain a high level of dissemination of scholarship as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications and presentations at national and international meetings.</li><li>Provide leadership in innovative and emerging teaching pedagogies, national and/or international professional organizations, and in service to the college through faculty mentorship.</li><li>Serve on college and University committees.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><div>Perform other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS:<br></strong><br></div><div>The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions.<br><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><br></div><div><strong>REQUIRED:<br></strong><br></div><div>1. PhD degree.<br><br></div><div>2. Recognized leader in the field at a national/international level (e.g., Fellow in the AAN or AANP).<br><br></div><div>3. Eligible for tenure in the College of Nursing.<br><br></div><div>4. Experience teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels.<br><br></div><div>5. Research record evidenced by significant external funding (e.g. NIH, AHRQ).<br><br></div><div>6. Evidence of publications in established journals.<br><br></div><div>7. Proficiency in written communication skills.<br><br></div><div>8. Proficiency in oral communication skills.<br><br></div><div>9. Strong interpersonal skills.<br><br></div><div>10. Clinical expertise in area of specialization.<br><br></div><div>11. Expertise in palliative/end-of-life, community/public health, pediatrics, psychiatric-mental health, gerontology, environmental health, or other area complementary to the faculty and college needs.<br><br></div><div>12. Ability to write competitive applications for extramural funding.<br><br></div><div>13. Eligible for RN or APRN licensure in Rhode Island.<br><br></div><div>14. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations.<br><br></div><div><strong>PREFERRED:</strong></div><div><br></div><ul><li>Evidence of successful research collaborations.</li></ul><div><br>_______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br></div><div><strong>URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship<br>university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative<br>workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts.<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status.<br>Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711.<br></strong><br></div> Dean Nursing https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16783 2026-06-22T16:11:06-04:00 2026-06-22T16:11:08-04:00 Academic Advisor <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by July 15, 2026. Applications received after July 15, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>THE OPPORTUNITY FOR A REMOTE/HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE IS POSSIBLE AFTER SIX MONTHS.</strong> <br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:</strong><br><br>Serve as liaison to all new and continuing transfer students in the College of Arts and Sciences, ensuring them easy navigation of the University’s academic programs. Work with the college’s Student Academic Services team to provide support for all transfer students and for faculty, staff, and administration who serve those students.</div><div><br></div> Dean Arts & Sciences https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17009 2026-08-29T17:02:13-04:00 2026-08-29T17:02:13-04:00 Cook's Helper (3 Positions, Part-Time, 18 hrs., Academic Year) Dining Central Operations https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16887 2026-07-27T14:57:27-04:00 2026-07-27T14:57:28-04:00 Assistant Professor, Nursing (Palliative Care) <div><br><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. <br>________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br>Campus Location: Nursing Education Center, Providence or main campus, Kingston<br><br><br>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br><br>_______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br>The College of Nursing is searching for an Assistant Professor, tenure track position to begin in Fall 2026.</div><div><br>The College of Nursing has over 850 undergraduate nursing students and 120 graduate students in our MS, post-masters MS Certificate, and post-masters DNP, and PhD programs. The College of Nursing includes the Kingston campus (undergraduate program) and the additional location of the Rhode Island Nursing Education Center (NEC) in Providence (graduate program and upper division undergraduate course work). Both locations provide opportunities for clinical skills and simulation learning as well as interdisciplinary research and collaborations.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:</strong></div><div><br>The College of Nursing (CON) is committed to scientific inquiry, knowledge development, and excellence in teaching. We are building a faculty with a strong research focus to support our mission to prepare outstanding and compassionate nurses to excel as clinicians, scholars, and leaders who will enhance the health care of individuals, families, communities, and populations both locally and globally. The successful candidate will have a background in palliative care with a research focus in this area. Palliative care research focus is important, and may include symptom science, chronic disease, and quality of life, etc. The successful candidate will have an appointment to the College of Nursing with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the campus including the health-related Colleges of Health Science, and Pharmacy, the Ryan Institute for Neurosciences, as well as external partners. The candidate will be expected to establish a program of research that complements the college's mission and is supported by extramural funding. The successful candidate will also contribute to palliative care initiatives within the college and beyond, the University's teaching mission, and participate in service activities.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Establish and maintain a robust program of research in palliative care and germane to nursing and health that is supported by extramural funding.</li><li>Maintain a high level of scholarly activity as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications and presentations at national and international meetings.</li><li>Contribute to the undergraduate and graduate teaching missions of the University by mentoring students and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses as assigned.</li><li>Service to the college, university, and profession.</li></ul><div><br><strong>OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><div>Perform other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS:</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions.<br><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><br></div><div><strong>REQUIRED:<br></strong><br></div><div>1. PhD degree or other research degree at time of appointment.<br><br></div><div>2. Master’s degree in nursing.<br><br></div><div>3. CV­ potential for/actual research, scholarship, and teaching effectiveness.<br><br></div><div>4. Strong interpersonal and oral communication skills.<br><br></div><div>5. Proficiency in writing skills.<br><br></div><div>6. Clinical expertise in palliative care.<br><br></div><div>7. Eligible for RN or APRN licensure in Rhode Island.<br><br></div><div>8. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations.</div><div><br><strong>PREFERRED:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Postdoctoral training related to program of research in the focus area.<br><br></li><li>Demonstrated experience in classroom and/or clinical teaching.<br><br></li><li>Evidence of successful research collaborations.<br><br></li><li>Demonstrated ability to write competitive applications for extramural funding.</li></ul><div><br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br>For inquiries about the position or the application process, please contact Faculty search chair: Dr. Diane DiTomasso (<a href=\"mailto:dditomasso@uri.edu\"><strong>dditomasso@uri.edu</strong></a> ) <br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts.<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711.<br></strong><br></div> Dean Nursing https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16482 2026-03-18T14:15:22-04:00 2026-03-18T14:15:23-04:00 Associate/Full Professor; Department Chair and Program Director - Physical Therapy <div><br><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. <br></strong><br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br>The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for a tenure-track Professor or Associate Professor who will serve as Department Chair and Program Director in Physical Therapy. We are looking for a leader with extensive experience in teaching and scholarship who complements the mission of the Department, College, and University. Appointment will be made at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, depending on qualifications. <strong>The position is a calendar-year appointment with a start date of August 2026.<br></strong><br>The well-established Physical Therapy Department is located within the College of Health Sciences. It is recognized for excellence in teaching, research, service, professional leadership, strong clinical education partners, and an on-site physical therapy clinic. Annually, a cohort of 32 DPT students are accepted and taught by a dedicated and experienced faculty. The Department's faculty leads several research laboratories to conduct research in motor control, exercise science, mobility assessment, and rehabilitation across various populations. Faculty are affiliates of the Ryan Institute of Neuroscience, Interdisciplinary Neuroscience Program, Rhode Island Geriatric Education Center, and Rhode Island Collaborative for lnterprofessional Education and Practice.<br>Faculty also recruit and advise graduate students from the PhD in Health Science program which has a specialty in physical therapy, the Interdisciplinary Neuroscience Program, and Kinesiology, Psychology, and Biomedical Engineering departments.<br><br>The Department, College, and University recognize that the field of physical therapy needs to be strengthened by contributions from a broad range of perspectives. The Department of Physical Therapy is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion and seeks to serve as a representative inspiration for the next generations. As such, we particularly welcome candidates from groups historically underrepresented, marginalized, and/or excluded in the field of physical therapy who will support the mission of both URI and the Department of Physical Therapy to expose students to different perspectives. Candidates will demonstrate a commitment to inclusivity to enhance a sense of belonging and academic success among students from diverse cultures and backgrounds.<br><br><strong>Duties and Responsibilities: <br><br></strong>The successful Department Chair and Program Director candidate will be expected to lead and administer for the Department with oversight of: fiscal, curricular, personnel, outcome<br>assessment, and accreditation components based on a shared vision aligned to the missions of the Department, College, University, and APTA; mentor and support the professional development of faculty and students (DPT and PhD); contribute directly to the delivery of the DPT curriculum; foster links with academic and professional colleagues on campus and throughout the community; and be active in the APTA and ACAPT. In general, individuals who will contribute to the Department’s commitment to scholarship, evidence-based practice, collaborative and inclusive teaching, and who strongly advocate for the Department are encouraged to apply.<br><br><strong>Major</strong> <strong>Responsibilities: <br><br></strong><strong><em>Leadership in Academic Excellence:</em></strong><br>● Serves as a direct liaison between the academic functions of the DPT program and the <br>business functions and provides strategic direction for maximizing resources and efficiency. Identifies resources required for the implementation of the strategic plan and potential obstacles that need to be addressed.<br>● Provides innovative leadership and ensures the integrity of the academic programs.<br>● Leads program curricula planning, implementation, evaluation, and revision in collaboration with the faculty.<br>● When appropriate, represents the DPT at the college and university levels and leads <br>DPT implementation of university-wide initiatives related to academic affairs, such as those to promote greater diversity and inclusion among graduate students.<br>● Determines faculty needs to support current and future academic programs.<br>● Provides support to effectively and efficiently align faculty with academic programs, teaching activities, and career development.<br>● Assures accountability in academic programs for effective utilization of all capital, personnel, <br>and revenue resources for priorities and budget forecasts for the academic mission.<br>● Represents the DPT on various DPT and University committees and serves as a liaison across<br> the university, providing leadership and strategy for DPT’s engagement in campus-wide initiatives.<br><br><strong><em>Faculty Recruitment and Development:</em></strong><br>● Cascades DPT’s strategy/mission statement throughout the organization for maximal alignment and develops appropriate rewards/recognition and coaching/corrective practices to align personnel with DPT goals.<br>● Leads strategic planning, implementation, and evaluation of initiatives to determine teaching needs, and provides strategic leadership for faculty development, mentoring, and recruitment.<br>● Collaborates with faculty, staff, college administrators, University resources, and Student Affairs to develop faculty abilities to work with students with diverse learning needs.<br>● Oversees the orientation of part-time faculty.<br><br><strong><em>Administration and Management:</em></strong><br>● With the aim of financial stability, assists the Dean to marshal limited resources to the most productive uses and identifies potential areas for revenue generation.<br>● Drives performance measures for the operation (including a consideration of efficiency <br>versus effectiveness).<br>● Identifies needed infrastructure and secures resources to support academic programs.<br>● Responsible for identifying the faculty and staff needs to support the academic programs and ensuring judicious use of these human resources.<br><br><strong>Qualifications<br><br>Required: </strong><br><br>1) A PhD or equivalent terminal academic degree.<br><br>2) Record of teaching, research and service commensurate with a tenured faculty appointment at the rank of associate or full professor.<br><br>3) Eligible for physical therapist licensure in Rhode Island.<br><br>4) Experience in teaching graduate students in a clinical program.<br><br>5) Experience in securing funding for research.<br><br>6) Demonstrated proficiency in oral communication skills.<br><br>7) Demonstrated experience in working with diverse groups/populations.<br><br>8) Current APTA membership.<br><br><strong>Preferred:</strong><br><br>1) Experience as a Department Chair, Program Director, or a comparable leadership position.<br><br>2) Demonstrated experience in interdepartmental and interdisciplinary collaboration.<br><br>3) Demonstrated knowledge or experience with accreditation processes, including outcome assessment.<br><br>4) Demonstrated competence in professional fiscal management.<br><br>5) Demonstrated successful teaching in areas that complement the existing curriculum.<br><br>6) Demonstrated research in areas that complement existing programs and foci in the Department, College of Health Sciences, and/or other affiliated entities.<br><br>7) Demonstrated experience in graduate student and junior faculty mentoring.<br><br>8) Evidence of leadership in obtaining successful CAPTE accreditation.<br><br>9) Demonstrated success in securing external research funding.<br><br>10) Demonstrate a strong scholarship record.<br><br>11) Demonstrated professional involvement at the state, national, or international level.<br><br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>The University of Rhode Island is an equal-opportunity employer. It is the policy of the University of Rhode Island to provide reasonable accommodation when requested by a qualified applicant or employee with a disability.<br></strong><br></div> Physical Therapy https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16788 2026-06-23T14:30:40-04:00 2026-06-23T14:30:41-04:00 Director of Operations, Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute (OECI) <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by July 6, 2026. Applications received after July 6, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. <br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI:<br><br></strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston and New York City.</div><div>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>POSTING SUMMARY:</strong><br><br>Oversee daily operations of the Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute (OECI). Chair the OECI Council of Fellows and assist with developing and executing the vision of the Principal Investigators. Coordinate the development of operational plans and timelines that are supported by the OECI affiliates. Be responsible for the development and implementation of plans and timelines for both external and internal OECI initiatives. Supervise the URI OECI staff, provide work priorities, and lead all personnel actions.<br><br></div> GSO Research https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17013 2026-08-31T13:42:21-04:00 2026-08-31T13:42:22-04:00 Assistant Dean, Pharmacy <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by September 18, 2026. Applications received after September 18, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br><br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY: </strong><br><br></div><div>Oversee the operation and development of metrics for the Student Services division of the Dean’s Office of the College of Pharmacy.<br><br></div><div>Primary responsibilities include: (1) Overseeing recruitment and advising undergraduate and professional students with their programs of study as they enter the College, transfer and seek readmission, and prepare for graduation.<br><br></div><div>(2) troubleshooting and resolving student academic issues, including scholastic, transfer, and graduation issues; (3) working with College administrators, via e-campus queries, provide institutional research services for the College; and (4) as needed, provide e-campus training and support for College faculty members and staff. As required, will teach one course.<br><br><br></div> Dean Pharmacy https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16889 2026-07-27T14:58:53-04:00 2026-07-27T14:58:53-04:00 Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing <div><br><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. <br>________________________________________________________________________________________________</strong><br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br>The College of Nursing is searching for a faculty member for a clinical track position to begin in Fall 2026. Experience in clinical nursing practice is required.<br><br></div><div><strong>POSTING SUMMARY: </strong><br><br></div><div>The College of Nursing (CON) is committed to excellence in teaching, scientific inquiry, and knowledge development. We are seeking a faculty member who will embrace our new college tagline, “Nurse leaders transforming wellbeing and environments,” and who has a strong record of clinical expertise that supports our mission. Our mission is to prepare nurses to excel as outstanding and compassionate clinicians, scholars, and leaders who will enhance the health and healthcare of individuals, families, communities, and populations both locally and globally. The successful candidate will have an appointment with the College of Nursing with primary responsibilities in clinical teaching, with possible classroom teaching, at the undergraduate and graduate levels as appropriate. The candidate will be expected to conduct teaching in clinical, collaborate for placements for students, and collaborate regarding faculty/preceptors as appropriate, participate in student advising and service to the college, and contribute to scholarly activities.<br><br><strong>KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Contribute as appropriate to the university's undergraduate and graduate teaching missions by teaching clinical and other courses as assigned, while mentoring students for the college.</li><li>Contribute to scholarship.</li><li>Service as an advisor, mentor, and professional role model to students.</li><li>Service to the college, university, and professional organizations.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><div>Perform other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS:<br></strong><br></div><div>The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions.<br><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><strong><br>REQUIRED:<br></strong><br></div><div>1. Ph.D. or DNP degree at the time of appointment.<br><br></div><div>2. Proficiency in written communication skills.<br><br></div><div>3. Proficiency in oral communication skills.<br><br></div><div>4. Strong interpersonal skills.<br><br></div><div>5. Clinical expertise in nursing.<br><br></div><div>6. Eligible for RN and/or APRN licensure in Rhode Island.<br><br></div><div>7. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations.<br><br><strong>PREFERRED:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Clinical practice experience in pediatrics, but open to other areas of clinical expertise.</li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li>Demonstrated experience in clinical and classroom teaching.</li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li>Evidence and potential for clinical scholarship.<br><br></li></ul><div>______________________________________________________________________________________________________</div><div><br><strong>URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship<br>university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative<br>workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts.<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status.<br>Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting<br>the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711.<br></strong><br></div> Dean Nursing https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16514 2026-03-18T14:16:41-04:00 2026-03-18T14:16:41-04:00 Associate/Full Professor, PhD Program Director - Human Development & Family Science <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by April 4, 2026. Applications received after April 4, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>Position Summary:</strong><br><br>The Department of Human Development &amp; Family Science at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor who will also serve as the Program Director for the PhD in Health Sciences, an interdisciplinary program in the College of Health Sciences. We are looking for a leader with extensive experience obtaining external funding for research and mentoring graduate students and who complements the mission of the Department, College, and University. We have a particular emphasis on applied research aimed at improving the quality of life for individuals, families, and communities. Appointment will be made at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, depending on qualifications. The position is a 9-month appointment. We seek an accomplished scholar whose research and teaching address early stages of development across the lifespan and child health. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: child health and well-being, connections between physical and mental health, child life and pediatric health services, lifespan development, and medical social work.</div><div><br>The Human Development &amp; Family Science Department is located within the College of Health Sciences and is recognized for excellence in teaching, research, service, and experiential education. The Department includes high quality outreach programs, including child development centers and couple and family therapy clinics. The Department’s faculty lead several research laboratories/programs, conducting research in individual and family wellness across the lifespan. The PhD in Health Sciences is an interdisciplinary program with specializations in physical therapy, kinesiology, nutrition, communicative disorders, and human development &amp; family science. <br><br>The Department, College, and University recognize the importance of contributions from a broad range of perspectives. The Department of Human Development &amp; Family Science is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion and seeks to serve as a representative inspiration for the next generations. As such, we particularly welcome candidates from groups historically underrepresented, marginalized, and/or excluded in the field of human development &amp; family science who will support the mission of both URI and the College of Health Sciences to expose students to different perspectives. Candidates will demonstrate a commitment to inclusivity to enhance a sense of belonging and academic success among students from diverse cultures and backgrounds.<br><br><strong>Qualifications<br><br>Required:</strong><br><br>1. A PhD or equivalent terminal academic degree in human development &amp; family science, social work, or a closely related field. <br><br>2. Record of teaching, research, and service commensurate with a tenured faculty appointment at the rank of associate or full professor.<br><br>3. Experience in teaching and mentoring graduate students, including PhD students.<br><br>4. Track record of successfully securing external research funding and having a strong scholarship record.<br><br>5. Strong leadership, teamwork, organizational, and communication skills.<br><br>6. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations.<br><br><strong>Preferred:</strong></div><div><br>1. Clinical background with licensure (e.g., social work or related professional license).<br><br>2. Leadership experience in graduate education.<br><br>3. Experience in human development and family science programs.<br><br>4. Demonstrated experience in interdepartmental and interdisciplinary collaboration.<br><br>5. Demonstrated successful teaching in areas of family and community health and early lifespan development.<br><br>6. Experience working within medical or healthcare systems.<br><br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>EEO Statement:<br></strong><br></div><div>URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711.</div><div><br></div> Human Development & Family Science https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16793 2026-06-24T14:55:30-04:00 2026-06-24T14:55:31-04:00 Executive Assistant I <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by July 18, 2026. Applications received after July 18, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>POSTING SUMMARY: </strong><br><br>Report directly to the Dean of the College of Arts &amp; Sciences, providing critical administrative support and performing private administrative duties of a complex, confidential and responsible nature.<br><br></div> Dean Arts & Sciences https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17015 2026-08-31T16:17:50-04:00 2026-08-31T16:17:50-04:00 Cook's Helper (Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year) Dining Central Operations https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16895 2026-07-29T12:44:33-04:00 2026-07-29T12:44:34-04:00 Assistant Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice <div><strong>The search will remain open until the position has been filled. </strong>First consideration will be given to applications received by August 12, 2026.<strong> </strong>Applications received after August 12, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>About URI: </strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br>The University of Rhode Island College of Pharmacy invites applications for a full-time, academic-year (9-month), non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor position in the Department of Pharmacy Practice and Clinical Research. The position will contribute to the College’s teaching, clinical practice, service, and scholarly missions, with primary teaching responsibilities in the Pharmacy Practice and Care Process (PPCP)/Integrated Pharmacy Laboratory (IPL) sequence, Capstone courses, and other clinical courses within the Doctor of Pharmacy curriculum as needed.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will establish and maintain a clinical practice site in a clinic or ambulatory care setting that supports the expansion of pharmacist-provided patient care services, particularly for rural, underserved, and marginalized populations. The faculty member will also engage in service to the Department, College, University, profession, and community and pursue scholarly activities related to clinical practice, pharmacy education, community engagement, health disparities, or other areas aligned with the faculty member’s expertise and interests.<br><br>The anticipated start date is September 1, 2026. This is a full-time, academic year, non-tenure-track, limited, renewable appointment, with continuation contingent upon successful performance review and programmatic needs.<br><br><br><strong>KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Teaching and Mentorship<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Deliver instruction and facilitate active learning in the Pharmacy Practice and Care Process (PPCP)/Integrated Pharmacy Laboratory (IPL) sequence (I–V).</li><li>Lead and support skills-based education, including patient counseling and communication, prescription processing and clinical decision-making, drug information and medication therapy management, sterile and non-sterile compounding, physical assessment, and point-of-care skills.</li><li>Contribute to Capstone courses through case-based instruction, simulation activities, student assessment, course coordination, and activities designed to prepare students for Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiences (APPEs) and contemporary pharmacy practice.</li><li>Deliver instruction in other required and elective clinical courses within the Doctor of Pharmacy curriculum based on departmental and programmatic needs and the faculty member’s areas of expertise.</li><li>Facilitate recitations, simulations, case-based learning activities, and interprofessional education experiences.</li><li>Assess student performance through skills-based assessments, Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs), written assignments, care plans, and other appropriate assessment methods.</li><li>Provide timely feedback, remediation, coaching, and mentorship to support student development and professional growth.</li><li>Contribute to course and curricular assessment, continuous quality improvement, and curriculum development.</li><li>Oversee and mentor Teaching Assistants, pharmacy residents, and other learners assigned to relevant courses and educational activities.</li><li>Precept Doctor of Pharmacy students completing experiential education rotations.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Clinical Practice and Professional Service<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Establish and maintain a high-quality clinical practice site in collaboration with a partnering clinic or healthcare organization.</li><li>Develop, implement, and evaluate pharmacist-provided patient care services designed to improve medication use, health outcomes, and access to care.</li><li>Provide direct patient care services within the scope of pharmacist practice and applicable state laws and regulations.</li><li>Collaborate with physicians, pharmacists, nurses, social workers, community health workers, and other healthcare professionals to provide patient-centered, team-based care.</li><li>Support initiatives designed to expand access to pharmacist-provided services for rural, underserved, marginalized, and other populations experiencing barriers to healthcare.</li><li>Develop a clinical practice environment that provides opportunities for student pharmacists, pharmacy residents, and other health professions learners.</li><li>Contribute professional expertise to community organizations, healthcare partners, professional associations, and other external stakeholders as appropriate.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Scholarship<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Develop and maintain a program of scholarly activity consistent with the expectations of a non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor.</li><li>Pursue internal and external funding opportunities to support clinical practice innovation, pharmacy education, community-engaged initiatives, healthcare access, health equity, or other areas aligned with the faculty member’s expertise and interests.</li><li>Disseminate scholarly work through peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, reports, educational scholarship, or other appropriate scholarly products.</li><li>Collaborate with faculty, students, healthcare professionals, and community partners on scholarly and grant-funded initiatives.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>College, University, and Professional Service<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Participate in departmental, College, and University governance and service activities, including appointment to standing and ad hoc committees.</li><li>Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement initiatives.</li><li>Participate in faculty meetings, strategic planning activities, student recruitment, and other activities supporting the missions of the Department and College.</li><li>Engage in service to professional organizations, healthcare organizations, community partners, or other external organizations as appropriate.</li><li>Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and external partners to advance the teaching, practice, service, and scholarly missions of the College.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><div>Perform other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS:<br></strong><br></div><div>The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions.<br><br><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>REQUIRED:<br><br></strong>1. Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) degree from an ACPE-accredited college or university.<br><br>2. Completion of a PGY1 pharmacy residency.<br><br>3. Minimum of three years of pharmacy practice experience.<br><br>4. Licensed or eligible for pharmacist licensure in Rhode Island. <br><br>5. Experience providing direct patient care and applying the Pharmacists’ Patient Care Process.<br><br>6. Experience precepting student pharmacists or other health professions learners.<br><br>7. Demonstrated strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. <br><br>8. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, healthcare professionals, community partners, and interprofessional teams.<br><br>9. Demonstrated effective teaching, presentation, and facilitation skills.<br><br>10. Demonstrated commitment to working effectively with diverse populations and fostering inclusive learning and clinical practice environments.<br><br><strong>PREFERRED:</strong></div><div><br>1. Prior didactic, laboratory, or experiential teaching experience in a Doctor of Pharmacy or other health professions program.<br><br>2. Experience providing care to rural, underserved, marginalized, or other populations experiencing barriers to healthcare.<br><br>3. Experience providing pharmacist services under a Collaborative Practice Agreement (CPA) or other collaborative patient care model.<br><br>4. Experience coordinating courses, laboratory sequences, simulations, or large-scale student assessments.<br><br>5. Evidence of scholarly productivity or demonstrated potential for scholarly contributions.<br><br>6. Experience developing, implementing, expanding, or evaluating pharmacist-provided patient care services.<br><br>7. APhA Pharmacy-Based Immunization Delivery certification or willingness to obtain certification.<br><br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________</div><div><br><strong>EEO Statement:<br></strong><br></div><div>URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711.</div><div><br></div> Dean Pharmacy https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16521 2026-03-18T14:17:01-04:00 2026-03-18T14:17:01-04:00 Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program <h1>The search will remain open until the position has been filled.</h1><div><strong>________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br></strong>Qualified candidates who are not selected for employment for fall semester 2024 will have their applications remain active for two (2) years should a future opportunity arise during the 2025–2026 instructional year, September 1, 2025–August 31, 2026.<br><br>The Department of Professional and Public Writing in the Harrington School of Communication and Media and College of Arts and Sciences seeks part-time faculty to teach online graduate courses for the UX Graduate Certificate Program on a per-course basis. Areas of instruction include ethical foundations of UX design, UX research and methods, UX and microcopy writing, and interaction design.<br><br></div><div>As the largest college at the University of Rhode Island, the College of Arts and Sciences brings together and supports undergraduate programs across the arts, humanities, sciences, and social sciences. The college is committed to excellence in teaching and its academic units create learning experiences that stress the free and rigorous pursuit of knowledge, intellectual curiosity, respect for differences across cultures and perspectives, a passion for personal expression, and an investment in the responsibilities of an educated global citizen in a democratic society. The College facilitates students' development into leaders and global citizens who think critically and creatively, communicate effectively, and participate actively in local and global communities.<br><br><br></div><div><strong>DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong><br></div><div>A selected candidate will teach one (1) or two (2) courses in the Department of Professional and Public Writing. Courses are asynchronous and delivered in an accelerated 7-week format. Part-time faculty are not required to engage in research or service activities but must hold regular office hours and be available to assist students enrolled in their courses. They are expected to stay current in their fields of instruction and with pedagogical methods and instructional technologies. Online teaching requires certification and possibly training by the University. Courses are three (3) credits. Specific responsibilities include:<br><br></div><ul><li>Delivering online lessons and assignments in UX Design principles, tools, and techniques through our course management platform (Brightspace)</li><li>Providing regular feedback, guidance, and mentoring support to students to facilitate their learning and skill development while conveying confidence in every student's ability to learn</li><li>Cultivating a collaborative and participatory online learning environment that values diversity of people, ideas, cultures, and forms of expression</li><li>Evaluating student performance and progress and providing timely assessment</li><li>Fostering a safe environment that respects the diversity of people and ideas by modeling respect for all students and conveying confidence in every student's ability to learn</li></ul><div><strong><br><br>Qualifications:<br><br>Required:<br><br></strong>1. Master's degree in technical communication or related field or a bachelor's degree and three (3) years of professional experience in areas such as UX research, UX analytics, UX writing and/or content design, usability and heuristic evaluation, accessibility, wireframing/prototyping, and/or content optimization and strategy.<br><br></div><div>2. Must have technical knowledge and proficiency in interaction design technologies (e.g., Figma) and the Adobe Suite, as well as remote collaboration tools.<br><br><strong>Preferred:</strong></div><div><strong><br></strong>1.<strong> </strong>Teaching experience at the college level.<br><br></div><div>2. For candidates with master’s degrees, professional experience in the field of UX.<br><br>______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>The University of Rhode Island is an equal-opportunity employer. It is the policy of the University of Rhode Island to provide reasonable accommodation when requested by a qualified applicant or employee with a disability.</strong></div><div><br></div> Professional & Public Writing https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17019 2026-09-01T13:56:37-04:00 2026-09-01T13:56:37-04:00 Coordinator, Compliance (NCAA) and Athletics Administration <div><strong>About URI: <br><br></strong>The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City.<br>________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br><br><strong>Position is In-person.<br><br>POSITION SUMMARY:<br><br></strong>Under the direction of the Deputy Athletic Director/ COO and Chief NCAA Compliance Officer and working with the Associate Athletic Director Team, the basic function of the Coordinator, Compliance and Athletics Administration is to provide hands on operational, administrative, academic and NCAA compliance support in the day-to-day activities of a fast-paced D1 Athletic Program.<br><br></div> Athletics Administration https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/1