    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17032": {
      "title": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Landscape Maintenance Technician III",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Landscape Maintenance Technician III Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Landscape Maintenance Technician III Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: At the time of appointment and continually thereafter as a condition of continued employment: 1. Must possess a valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL), Class B 2. Must possess a valid Arborist License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM) 3. Must possess a valid Rhode Island Commercial Pesticide Applicator’s license as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM) 4. Must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician’s certificate 5. Must possess a Hoisting License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Labor & Training (DLT) Posting Details Position Information Posting Number CS02304 Job Title Landscape Maintenance Technician III Position Number TBD FTE 1.00 FLSA Pay Rate Salary Range $59,684 - $68,574 Pay Grade Level 324A Position Type Classified Civil Service Staff Union C94/L528 - Council 94/Local 528 (Serv/Maint) Status Full-time, Calendar Year, Permanent Restriction or Limitation Reason End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Landscape & Grounds Maintenance Contact(s) Sean Nelson Specialist, Talent Acquisition Office of Human Resource Administration 80 Lower College Road Kingston, RI 02881 Contact Phone/Extension 401-874-5269 Contact Email sean.nelson@uri.edu Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Building(s) Grant Funded Extension Contingent on Funding Date Extension Contingency Notes Duties and Responsibilities ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLES OF WORK PERFORMED : Within the University of Rhode Island ( URI ), to perform and oversee advanced technical and skilled work, including computation of quantities, quality, cost, estimating labor and materials relating to landscape projects at URI and all the properties owned by URI ; to be responsible for and train subordinates on: maintenance of equipment, the application of general use pesticides, professional tree work, planting, watering, sweeping, snow removal, and the utilization of plants used to beautify the university properties; and to do related work as required. To supervise subordinates engaged in cleaning and maintaining parking lots, roadsides, landscape plantings, including transplanting shrubs or trees, pruning trees, tree stump removal, tree stump grinding, weeding, spraying, fertilizing, hydroseeding, rolling and sodding, leaf collection, trimming and mowing grass. To be responsible for the maintenance of shrubbery and other plant materials used to beautify landscape beds, bioretention ponds, swales, slope coverages, parking lots and roadsides. To maintain current knowledge and specific care needs of various plants including trees, shrubs and perennials. To be involved in plant material selection, including plant identification and calculations of quantities for various planting and landscape projects. To supervise maintenance subordinates in special roadside projects such as selective tree and planting projects and appropriate herbicide application procedures dealing with both planted and native flora and fauna. To recommend landscape planting for site improvements and erosion control including grading, filling, sloping, selection of proper plant materials to combat the erosion, seeding and sodding. To perform safety sensitive functions and provide a safe work environment for co-workers and the campus community by following established work and safety rules. As assigned, to operate heavy trucks equipped with plow blades and spreaders to remove snow and ice and spread de-icing materials on sidewalks, parking lots and roadway surfaces. As assigned, to operate mowers or tractors with attached rotary, gang, sickle or other type cutters to control vegetation in ditches, medians and other areas of university owned right-of-way. To operate turf management equipment such as aerator, top-dressing attachment, rototiller, sod cutter, and over seeding equipment. To operate watering equipment such as tow behind water buffalo, water tanks, truck mounted water tanks, hose and reel and other related equipment to maintain healthy plant material on the university campus. Required Qualifications KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS AND CAPACITIES : Advanced knowledge of industry standard landscape maintenance methods, practices and techniques and the ability to apply such methods, practices and techniques, including the safe use of appropriate equipment; advanced knowledge of arboriculture, turf maintenance and safe use of herbicides; knowledge of the methods commonly used in the eradication of insect pests and diseases of ornamental plants; the ability to lay out, coordinate and supervise the work of skilled and unskilled personnel; the ability to direct proper seeding, hydroseeding, sodding and fertilizing methods and practices; the ability to keep records and prepare written reports; the ability to follow oral and written instructions; and related capacities and abilities. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE : Education: Possession of associate degree or higher in Horticulture, Landscape Architecture, Plant Science, Forestry, or another related course study; and Experience: A minimum of seven (7) years of employment in public agency or in private industry involving arboriculture or landscape maintenance at a technical level, including possession of valid Pesticide and Arborist licenses for that duration. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to environmental conditions. Work Hours 7:30am – 4:00pm – Monday – Friday Saturday and Sunday off Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 09/14/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS : At the time of appointment and continually thereafter as a condition of continued employment: 1. Must possess a valid Commercial Driver’s License ( CDL ), Class B 2. Must possess a valid Arborist License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management ( DEM ) 3. Must possess a valid Rhode Island Commercial Pesticide Applicator’s license as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management ( DEM ) 4. Must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician’s certificate 5. Must possess a Hoisting License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Labor & Training ( DLT ) Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17031 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Required License Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a state employee who is a member of AFSCME/Council 94? yes no * Do you have advanced knowledge of industry standard landscape maintenance methods, practices and techniques and the ability to apply such methods, practices and techniques, including the safe use of appropriate equipment? (Open Ended Question) * Do you possess a valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL), Class B? yes no * Do you possess a valid Arborist License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM) ? yes no * Do you possess a valid Rhode Island Commercial Pesticide Applicator's license as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM)? yes no * Do you possess a Hoisting License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Labor & Training\r\n(DLT)? yes no To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/bookmarks?posting_id=17032": {
      "title": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Log In Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Your session has expired. Please log in. Log In Required fields are indicated with an asterisk * Username * Password * Forgot your username or password? Or Create an Account × The Chronicle of Higher Education had retired the \"Apply with Vitae\" login option. No need to worry, read on for steps to access your account. To access the account, return to the login page using the \"X\" in the upper corner or clicking outside of this pop-up box. Use the \"Forgot your username or password?\" link with your original Chronicle Vitae username to create a new password and access your account. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
