    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17016": {
      "title": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Computer Systems Administrator Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Computer Systems Administrator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02201 Job Title Computer Systems Administrator Position Number 107036 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level:  13 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $80,000 - $90,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dean Engineering Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by October 1, 2026. Applications received after October 1, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION IS ELIGIBLE FOR A HYBRID (50% REMOTE ALLOWABLE ) WORK SCHEDULE . POSITION SUMMARY : Manage and support computing, networking, instructional, and research technology for the Electrical and Computer Engineering department within the College of Engineering. Maintain Linux servers, workstations, research clusers, laboratories, embedded systems, FPGA platforms, engineering software, and related equipment. Approximately 80% of the position’s time supports the Electrical and Computer Engineering department. The remaining 20% support the College of Engineering computing needs as assigned. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Administer and maintain Linux servers, workstations, research clusters, teaching laboratories, embedded systems, FPGA platforms, printers, and related devices. Install, configure, upgrade, secure, monitor, document, and troubleshoot software, operating systems, databases, and network services. Provide preventive maintenance for safety and continued operation of hardware/software systems. Perform backups, recovery, patching, preventive maintenance, and lifecycle management to ensure reliable and secure operations. Support faculty, staff, and students with research computing, instructional technology, engineering software, laboratory systems, FPGA development, and embedded systems. Evaluate and improve computing systems to meet changing teaching, research, cybersecurity, and operational needs. Provide technical guidance, training, documentation, and remote-access support. Coordinate work with university personnel, vendors, consultants, and contractors. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Support College of Engineering computing systems, laboratories, instructional clusters, servers, workstations, and related technology as assigned. Assist with college-wide upgrades, deployments, troubleshooting, documentation, infrastructure projects, and integration with university systems. Provide backup technical support to other college units as needed. Maintain equipment, software, warranty, and supply inventories. Assist with technology planning, purchasing, deployment, replacement, and lifecycle scheduling. Perform additional duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Linux operating systems; physical and virtual servers; computers, research clusters; FPGAs; embedded systems; laboratory equipment; databases; backup, monitoring, scripting, programming, and engineering software. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1.Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science, information technology, or a related field. 2. Minimum two years of experience in an academic, research, or industrial setting involving Linux system administration, hardware, software, networking, FPGAs, embedded systems, or related engineering computing. 3. Demonstrated experience installing, administering, maintaining, and troubleshooting Linux systems, hardware, software. 4. Ability to design and support technical solutions, manage multiple priorities, work independently, and respond effectively to operational issues. 5. Strong interpersonal, verbal, written and technical skills. 6. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Experience in higher education, engineering, research, or laboratory computing. 2. Experience with virtualization, research clusters, storage, backup systems, databases, web services, scripting, automation, cybersecurity, instructional laboratories, or vendor coordination. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Occasional lifting, equipment installation, work in laboratories or equipment rooms, and after-hours support may be required. Posting Date 09/01/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17000 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science, information technology, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum two years of experience in an academic, research, or industrial setting involving Linux system administration, hardware, software, networking, FPGAs, embedded systems, or related engineering computing? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience installing, administering, maintaining, and troubleshooting Linux systems, hardware, software? Yes No * Do you have ability to design and support technical solutions, manage multiple priorities, work independently, and respond effectively to operational issues? Yes No * Do you have strong interpersonal, verbal, written and technical skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
