    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16891": {
      "title": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Specialist I, Instructional Design - (3- Positions)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Specialist I, Instructional Design - (3- Positions) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Specialist I, Instructional Design - (3- Positions) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02185 Job Title Specialist I, Instructional Design - (3- Positions) Position Number 109008, 109437, 109805 FTE .43 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 11 Pay Grade Range Hourly Pay Rate:  $ 31.25 - $33.65 (positions are PT -15-hours per week, calendar year, limited to 06/26/2027 with possible extension) Status Calendar Year, Part-time, Limited Department Information Department Provost for Academic Affairs Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes The positions are part-time (15 hours per week), calendar year, limited to 06/26/2027 with possible extension. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 8, 2026. Applications received after August 8, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The positions are immediately eligible for a remote work schedule. POSITION SUMMARY : Assist faculty with the design of fully online courses of the highest possible quality. Provide instructional design and instructional technology services and support to faculty. Assist faculty in the development of learner-centered materials and other course materials for use primarily in online courses. Provide instructional design and instructional technology services and support to faculty, online programs, and administrators. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Partner with faculty and subject matter experts to refine existing and design new courses to ensure the best practices for online course design and instruction are embedded into the learning experience: Develop instructional strategies using multimedia and current Web capabilities within the course platforms. Consult with faculty on new instructional initiatives and provide implementation of these technologies within the Brightspace platform for all courses within their jurisdiction. Facilitate faculty training on effective implementation of learning technologies in online course design and instructions. Assist the Director and Assistant Director of Online Education & Instructional Design and/or Specialist Il, Instructional Design to complete URI Online initiatives as assigned. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers and word processing, database management, learning management systems and spreadsheet software; multimedia hardware and software, web development; courseware development; Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite; video conferencing. Brightspace. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in Instructional Design or related field. 2. Minimum of two years of web and multimedia development experience, OR, Minimum of two years of experience in online teaching and/or online training. 3. Demonstrated experience working with faculty on course design & development for distance learning. 4. Demonstrated experience working with faculty on blended learning courses and programs. 5. Demonstrated knowledge and application of instructional design theory, instructional design principles, learning theory, instructional technology, and/or accessibility principles. 6. Demonstrated experience creating online courses and programs. 7. Demonstrated knowledge of best practices in academic fully online and blended course delivery technology areas. 8. Demonstrated knowledge of emerging multimedia and other technologies. 9. Demonstrated ability to work with new and unfamiliar technologies. 10. Demonstrated experience with the online learning platform (such as Brightspace). 11. Demonstrated experience in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite Applications. 12. Demonstrated experience in video conferencing and web development tools (such as Articulate 360). 13. Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills. 14. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 15. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Master’s degree in Instructional Design or related field. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 07/27/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16871 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Instructional Design or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of web and multimedia development experience, OR, minimum of two years of experience in online teaching and/or online training? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience working with faculty on course design & development for distance learning? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience working with faculty on blended learning courses and programs? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated knowledge and application of instructional design theory, instructional design principles, learning theory, instructional technology, and/or accessibility principles? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience creating online courses and programs? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated knowledge of best practices in academic fully online and blended course delivery technology areas? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated knowledge of emerging multimedia and other technologies? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with new and unfamiliar technologies? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with the online learning platform (such as Brightspace)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite Applications? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in video conferencing and web development tools (such as Articulate 360)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
